        <mxCell id="c124" value="A positive difference: the promotion earns more than it gives up at that discount and lift" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=12;fontColor=#2C3E50;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="492" width="520" height="20" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c125" value="&lt;i&gt;The inputs, in blue, are C38 and C39; they sit on this sheet because a data table&#x27;s input cells must. C40 is the result cell, selected, and B42 repeats it. Every grid cell is the one array formula {=TABLE(C38,C39)}. The shaded cells begin at the first lift above each break-even: 5% at 15%, 8% at 25%, 10% at 35%, 12% at 40%.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="521" width="860" height="53" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
